    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other two files are its base and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners in this Spring Boot PetClinic app. The request now accepts an optional `birthDate`, and reads return `ageBand` computed against `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (DTO source of truth, DTOs are generated at build):\n   - Added `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to `OwnerFields` \u2014 the optional request input.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` read model.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`birth_date` column) field with getter/setter so the value survives to read time.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(owner)` derivation mapped onto `OwnerDto`: computes complete years via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` \u2014 `MINOR` under 18, `ADULT` for 18\u201364, `SENIOR` for 65+; returns `null` (field absent) when no birth date is present. MapStruct maps `birthDate` from the request DTO automatically.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb used by tests, plus h2/mysql/postgres for consistency).\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`birthDate` `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ageBand` `ADULT`) passes, as does the whole suite (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
